report=(S/'review-list.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
summary=report.split('## Exact cache items')[0].split('\n',1)[1].strip()
body='Claudio: '+marker+'. YY explicitly asked for this list and then asked me to give it to you. **YY has NOT approved removal of this or any prior set. Nothing has been deleted, pruned, moved or untagged. Please review the exact dependencies and present the choices to YY before any deletion.**\n\n'+summary+'\n\n'
body+='The published [complete readable list]('+base+'review-list.md) includes every one of the 65 cache IDs, individual bytes, parent/child links and last use. The [exact JSON]('+base+'exact-review-list.json) and [publication index]('+base+'publication-index.json) retain the complete evidence bindings. Exact sortable lists: [65 cache records]('+base+'exact-build-cache-65-records.csv), [old backup options]('+base+'old-backup-options.csv), [unused image options and dependencies]('+base+'unused-image-options.csv), [three verified proof folders]('+base+'verified-proof-folder-options.csv).\n\n'
body+='**Backup distinction:** the two issue155/issue159 files retire distinct historical restore points; another exact copy has NOT been verified. They are older standalone backups, not the current DB or latest backup sets. No current configuration, retained release-authority input, open process file or container mount consumer was found in the inspected scope. Their removal still needs YY to accept losing those restore points. The failed_db file is different: its retained dev_pre_api_dialog218 counterpart is byte-identical by stable SHA-256. No backup contents were transferred or opened with SQLite.\n\n'
body+='**Held image dependencies:** the unused 15.275GB soilfer/lab:2026.10b is selected by the running hub LAB_IMAGE and deployment .env, so it stays. Manual-sync is still referenced by /opt/soilfer-learn/docker-compose.yml:74; temporalio/admin-tools:1.32.0 by /opt/alitt/docker-compose.yml:95. Historical LIMS images and the other previous Museum image remain held by the exact retained release/protection references shown in the image CSV. OCI manifest aliases were resolved: candidate1d has 15 stopped-container consumers and is excluded. No running production image is a removal option.\n\n'
body+='**Proof evidence:** all 93 actual files across ONLY metadata233000/020000/023000 were freshly stable-hashed and independently matched to published raw Git blobs; the [per-file verified-copy record]('+base+'proof-copies-verified-elsewhere.json) contains exact commits/paths/hashes. No current mount, process-open-file or selected release-input consumer was found. 050000 raw files, 060000 DB files, all unverified proof folders, current/next inputs, qualified build roots and all stopped containers are excluded. The earlier five-root card is not this list and grants no authority.\n\n'
body+='Fresh sanitized metadata windows were09:49:42–09:57:50UTC, including all76 containers, OCI image-manifest consumers, cache parent edges, 137 config/service/cron files and selected retained release authority/scripts. This does not prove absence of every external/manual consumer. Reference free space27,415,519,232B is not a fresh capacity gate. Docker cache/image values are accounting estimates, not guaranteed physical deletion deltas. No blanket prune is proposed; eventual exact-ID support and fresh state must be checked only after YY approves an exact set. **This handoff is read-only review, not cleanup authorization, a source PASS, a proof launch or a release gate.**'
(D/'posted-body.txt').write_text(body,encoding='utf-8');(D/'post-input.json').write_text(json.dumps({'body':body}),encoding='utf-8')
b=cmd('gh','api','--method','POST','repos/yigini/soilfer-lims/issues/162/comments','--input',str(D/'post-input.json'));(D/'post-response-original.json').write_bytes(b);v=json.loads(b);assert v['body']==body
(D/'delivery-record.json').write_text(json.dumps({'status':'ONE_EXACT_READ_ONLY_LIST_SENT_TO_CLAUDIO_NATIVE_PENDING','id':v['id'],'url':v['html_url'],'createdAt':v['created_at'],'listCommit':HEAD,'cleanupApproved':False,'neverRepeat':True},indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
print(json.dumps({'id':v['id'],'url':v['html_url'],'createdAt':v['created_at'],'deleted':0}))
